  "question": {
    "text": "The first transition series metal ' M ' has the highest enthalpy of atomisation in its series. One of its aquated ion $\\left(\\mathrm{M}^{\\mathrm{n} \\dagger}\\right)$ exists in green colour. The nature of the oxide formed by the above $\\mathrm{M}^{\\mathrm{n}-}$ ion is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HEQhG",
      "text": "neutral",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7Tcq9",
      "text": "acidic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ShIxU",
      "text": "basic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
